IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg2-support`
IMPORT `dg2-registered-agent`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: sections 133 to 136 -- CHANGING THE REGISTERED OFFICE OR AGENT, THE AGENT'S CHANGE
-- OF ADDRESS OR NAME, AND THE AGENT'S RESIGNATION (with or without a successor).
--
-- SEAT: a director or officer whose board changes the registered office or agent, or whose agent resigns; a stockholder of a corporation whose
-- agent resigns. The Secretary of State is no seat: what the Secretary does is encoded as what follows for the corporation.
-- Cross-references taken as inputs: section 102(a)(2) and section 103 (piece dg1), section 321 (piece dg10), section 510 and 8 Del. C.
-- chapter 5 (not among the inputs). The text is de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (a plain-text rendering, not the official text).
-- Dates and periods are counted with the core's calendar arithmetic; the last day of a period of days is inside it (core Fork F3).

§ `Section 133: the board changes the registered office or agent`

-- "Any corporation may, by resolution of its board of directors, change the location of its registered office in this State to any other place in this State."
-- src:343 | Any corporation may, by resolution of its board of directors, change the location of its registered office in this State to any other place in this State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 133 (src:343)
GIVEN `the board of directors adopted a resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new place is in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 133 the corporation may change the location of its registered office` `the board of directors adopted a resolution` `the new place is in this State` MEANS
        `the board of directors adopted a resolution`
    AND `the new place is in this State`

-- "By like resolution, the registered agent of a corporation may be changed to any other person or corporation including itself."
-- Fork F-133-1: "any other person or corporation" is read together with section 132(a), which says who may be a registered agent, so the
-- new agent must be one section 132(a) allows; section 133 does not repeat the list.
-- src:343 | By like resolution, the registered agent of a corporation may be changed to any other person or corporation including itself. In either such case, the resolution shall be as detailed in its statement as is required by § 102(a)(2) of this title. Upon the adoption of such a resolution, a certificate certifying the change shall be executed, acknowledged, and filed in accordance with § 103 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 133 (src:343)
GIVEN `the board of directors adopted a resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new agent is a person or corporation other than the present registered agent, including the corporation itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new agent may be a registered agent under section 132(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 133 the corporation may change its registered agent` `the board of directors adopted a resolution` `the new agent is a person or corporation other than the present registered agent, including the corporation itself` `the new agent may be a registered agent under section 132(a)` MEANS
        `the board of directors adopted a resolution`
    AND `the new agent is a person or corporation other than the present registered agent, including the corporation itself`
    AND `the new agent may be a registered agent under section 132(a)`

-- "In either such case, the resolution shall be as detailed in its statement as is required by § 102(a)(2) of this title. Upon the adoption of
-- such a resolution, a certificate certifying the change shall be executed, acknowledged, and filed in accordance with § 103 of this title."
-- Whether the resolution is as detailed as section 102(a)(2) requires, and whether the certificate was executed, acknowledged and filed as
-- section 103 requires, are for piece dg1: facts here. The section does not say when the change takes effect.
-- src:343 | In either such case, the resolution shall be as detailed in its statement as is required by § 102(a)(2) of this title. Upon the adoption of such a resolution, a certificate certifying the change shall be executed, acknowledged, and filed in accordance with § 103 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 133 (src:343)
GIVEN `the board of directors adopted a resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133 the corporation must execute, acknowledge and file a certificate certifying the change` `the board of directors adopted a resolution` MEANS
    IF   `the board of directors adopted a resolution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- out of range: section 102(a)(2) (piece dg1): whether the resolution is as detailed as it requires is a plain input.
-- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1): how a certificate is executed, acknowledged and filed is theirs; whether it was is a plain input.
-- src:343 | In either such case, the resolution shall be as detailed in its statement as is required by § 102(a)(2) of this title. Upon the adoption of such a resolution, a certificate certifying the change shall be executed, acknowledged, and filed in accordance with § 103 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 133 (src:343)
GIVEN `the resolution is as detailed in its statement as section 102(a)(2) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate certifying the change was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with section 103` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 133 the corporation has done what the Law requires after the resolution` `the resolution is as detailed in its statement as section 102(a)(2) requires` `the certificate certifying the change was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with section 103` MEANS
        `the resolution is as detailed in its statement as section 102(a)(2) requires`
    AND `the certificate certifying the change was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with section 103`

§ `Section 134: the agent's change of address or name`

DECLARE `s 134(a) Facts about the registered agent's certificate` HAS
    `the person is the registered agent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the new address is in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the registered agent filed a certificate with the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate is executed and acknowledged by the registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate sets forth the address at which the agent has maintained the registered office for each of the corporations for which it is a registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate certifies the new address to which each registered office will be changed on a given day, and at which the agent will thereafter maintain the registered office for each corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the given day` IS A DATE
    `the date as of which the question is asked` IS A DATE

-- "A registered agent may change the address of the registered office of the corporation or corporations for which the agent is a registered
-- agent to another address in this State by filing with the Secretary of State a certificate, executed and acknowledged by such registered
-- agent, setting forth the address at which such registered agent has maintained the registered office for each of the corporations for
-- which it is a registered agent, and further certifying to the new address to which each such registered office will be changed on a given
-- day, and at which new address such registered agent will thereafter maintain the registered office for each of the corporations for
-- which it is a registered agent. Thereafter, or until further change of address, as authorized by law, the registered office in this State
-- of each of the corporations for which the agent is a registered agent shall be located at the new address of the registered agent thereof
-- as given in the certificate." TRUE from the given day if the certificate is as described; before then, or for a certificate that is not,
-- the text does not say where the office is: NOTHING.
-- src:347 | (a) A registered agent may change the address of the registered office of the corporation or corporations for which the agent is a registered agent to another address in this State by filing with the Secretary of State a certificate, executed and acknowledged by such registered agent, setting forth the address at which such registered agent has maintained the registered office for each of the corporations for which it is a registered agent, and further certifying to the new address to which each such registered office will be changed on a given day, and at which new address such registered agent will thereafter maintain the registered office for each of the corporations for which it is a registered agent. Thereafter, or until further change of address, as authorized by law, the registered office in this State of each of the corporations for which the agent is a registered agent shall be located at the new address of the registered agent thereof as given in the certificate.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 134(a) (src:347)
GIVEN f IS A `s 134(a) Facts about the registered agent's certificate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(a) the registered office of the corporation is located at the new address` f MEANS
    IF       f's `the person is the registered agent of the corporation`
         AND f's `the new address is in this State`
         AND f's `the registered agent filed a certificate with the Secretary of State`
         AND f's `the certificate is executed and acknowledged by the registered agent`
         AND f's `the certificate sets forth the address at which the agent has maintained the registered office for each of the corporations for which it is a registered agent`
         AND f's `the certificate certifies the new address to which each registered office will be changed on a given day, and at which the agent will thereafter maintain the registered office for each corporation`
         AND (f's `the date as of which the question is asked` AT LEAST f's `the given day`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (b): "In the event of a change of name of any person or corporation acting as registered agent in this State, such registered agent shall
-- file with the Secretary of State a certificate, executed and acknowledged by such registered agent, setting forth the new name of such
-- registered agent, the name of such registered agent before it was changed, and the address at which such registered agent has maintained
-- the registered office for each of the corporations for which it acts as a registered agent. A change of name of any person or corporation
-- acting as a registered agent as a result of a merger or consolidation of the registered agent, with or into another person or corporation
-- which succeeds to its assets by operation of law, shall be deemed a change of name for purposes of this section."
-- src:348 | (b) In the event of a change of name of any person or corporation acting as registered agent in this State, such registered agent shall file with the Secretary of State a certificate, executed and acknowledged by such registered agent, setting forth the new name of such registered agent, the name of such registered agent before it was changed, and the address at which such registered agent has maintained the registered office for each of the corporations for which it acts as a registered agent. A change of name of any person or corporation acting as a registered agent as a result of a merger or consolidation of the registered agent, with or into another person or corporation which succeeds to its assets by operation of law, shall be deemed a change of name for purposes of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 134(b) (src:348)
GIVEN `the name of the person or corporation acting as registered agent has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change of name is a result of a merger or consolidation of the registered agent with or into another person or corporation which succeeds to its assets by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(b) the registered agent must file a certificate of the change of name` `the name of the person or corporation acting as registered agent has changed` `the change of name is a result of a merger or consolidation of the registered agent with or into another person or corporation which succeeds to its assets by operation of law` MEANS
    IF   `the name of the person or corporation acting as registered agent has changed` OR `the change of name is a result of a merger or consolidation of the registered agent with or into another person or corporation which succeeds to its assets by operation of law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:348 | such registered agent shall file with the Secretary of State a certificate, executed and acknowledged by such registered agent, setting forth the new name of such registered agent, the name of such registered agent before it was changed, and the address at which such registered agent has maintained the registered office for each of the corporations for which it acts as a registered agent. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 134(b) (src:348)
GIVEN `the certificate is executed and acknowledged by the registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets forth the new name of the registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets forth the name of the registered agent before it was changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets forth the address at which the registered agent has maintained the registered office for each of the corporations for which it acts as a registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 134(b) the certificate of the change of name says what the Law requires` `the certificate is executed and acknowledged by the registered agent` `the certificate sets forth the new name of the registered agent` `the certificate sets forth the name of the registered agent before it was changed` `the certificate sets forth the address at which the registered agent has maintained the registered office for each of the corporations for which it acts as a registered agent` MEANS
        `the certificate is executed and acknowledged by the registered agent`
    AND `the certificate sets forth the new name of the registered agent`
    AND `the certificate sets forth the name of the registered agent before it was changed`
    AND `the certificate sets forth the address at which the registered agent has maintained the registered office for each of the corporations for which it acts as a registered agent`

§ `Section 135: resignation with the appointment of a successor`

-- "The registered agent of 1 or more corporations may resign and appoint a successor registered agent by filing a certificate with the
-- Secretary of State, stating the name and address of the successor agent, in accordance with § 102(a)(2) of this title. There shall be
-- attached to such certificate a statement of each affected corporation ratifying and approving such change of registered agent. Each such
-- statement shall be executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title. Upon such filing, the successor registered agent shall
-- become the registered agent of such corporations as have ratified and approved such substitution and the successor registered agent's
-- address, as stated in such certificate, shall become the address of each such corporation's registered office in this State."
-- For a corporation that did not ratify and approve, the successor does not become its registered agent.
-- out of range: section 102(a)(2) (piece dg1): whether the certificate states the name and address as it requires is part of this plain input.
-- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1): whether the statement is executed and acknowledged as it requires is a plain input.
-- src:352 | The registered agent of 1 or more corporations may resign and appoint a successor registered agent by filing a certificate with the Secretary of State, stating the name and address of the successor agent, in accordance with § 102(a)(2) of this title. There shall be attached to such certificate a statement of each affected corporation ratifying and approving such change of registered agent. Each such statement shall be executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title. Upon such filing, the successor registered agent shall become the registered agent of such corporations as have ratified and approved such substitution and the successor registered agent’s address, as stated in such certificate, shall become the address of each such corporation’s registered office in this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 135 (src:352)
GIVEN `the registered agent of the corporation filed a certificate with the Secretary of State stating the name and address of the successor agent in accordance with section 102(a)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement of the corporation ratifying and approving the change is attached to the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 135 the successor becomes the registered agent of the corporation and its address becomes the address of the corporation's registered office` `the registered agent of the corporation filed a certificate with the Secretary of State stating the name and address of the successor agent in accordance with section 102(a)(2)` `a statement of the corporation ratifying and approving the change is attached to the certificate` `the statement is executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103` MEANS
        `the registered agent of the corporation filed a certificate with the Secretary of State stating the name and address of the successor agent in accordance with section 102(a)(2)`
    AND `a statement of the corporation ratifying and approving the change is attached to the certificate`
    AND `the statement is executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103`

§ `Section 136: resignation without a successor`

-- (a): "The registered agent of a corporation, including a corporation which has become void pursuant to § 510 of this title, may resign
-- without appointing a successor by filing a certificate of resignation with the Secretary of State, but such resignation shall not become
-- effective until 30 days after the certificate is filed."
-- out of range: section 510 (8 Del. C. ch. 5, not among the inputs): whether the corporation has become void is a plain fact; the answer does not depend on it.
-- src:356 | The registered agent of a corporation, including a corporation which has become void pursuant to § 510 of this title, may resign without appointing a successor by filing a certificate of resignation with the Secretary of State, but such resignation shall not become effective until 30 days after the certificate is filed. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 136(a) (src:356)
GIVEN `the corporation has become void pursuant to section 510` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 136(a) the registered agent may resign without appointing a successor by filing a certificate of resignation` `the corporation has become void pursuant to section 510` MEANS
    TRUE

-- The resignation becomes effective 30 days after the certificate is filed (Fork F-136-1: on the thirtieth day after filing).
-- src:356 | but such resignation shall not become effective until 30 days after the certificate is filed. The certificate shall be executed and acknowledged by the registered agent, shall contain a statement that written notice of resignation was given to the corporation at least 30 days prior to the filing of the certificate by mailing or delivering such notice to the corporation at its address last known to the registered agent and shall set forth the date of such notice. The certificate shall include such information last provided to the registered agent pursuant to § 132(d) of this title for a communications contact for the affected corporation. Such information regarding the communications contact shall not be deemed public. A certificate filed pursuant to this section must be on the form prescribed by the Secretary of State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 136(a) (src:356)
GIVEN `the date the certificate of resignation is filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 136(a) the date the resignation becomes effective` `the date the certificate of resignation is filed` MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 30) `after` `the date the certificate of resignation is filed`

-- "The certificate shall be executed and acknowledged by the registered agent, shall contain a statement that written notice of resignation
-- was given to the corporation at least 30 days prior to the filing of the certificate by mailing or delivering such notice to the corporation
-- at its address last known to the registered agent and shall set forth the date of such notice. The certificate shall include such
-- information last provided to the registered agent pursuant to § 132(d) of this title for a communications contact for the affected
-- corporation. ... A certificate filed pursuant to this section must be on the form prescribed by the Secretary of State."
-- "At least 30 days prior to the filing": the notice date is at most the date 30 days before the filing date.
-- src:356 | The certificate shall be executed and acknowledged by the registered agent, shall contain a statement that written notice of resignation was given to the corporation at least 30 days prior to the filing of the certificate by mailing or delivering such notice to the corporation at its address last known to the registered agent and shall set forth the date of such notice. The certificate shall include such information last provided to the registered agent pursuant to § 132(d) of this title for a communications contact for the affected corporation. …
-- src:356 | A certificate filed pursuant to this section must be on the form prescribed by the Secretary of State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 136(a) (src:356)
GIVEN `the certificate is executed and acknowledged by the registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate contains a statement that written notice of resignation was given to the corporation by mailing or delivering it at its address last known to the registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets forth the date of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the notice` IS A DATE
      `the date the certificate is filed` IS A DATE
      `the certificate includes the information last provided to the registered agent pursuant to section 132(d) for a communications contact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is on the form prescribed by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 136(a) the certificate of resignation is as the Law requires` `the certificate is executed and acknowledged by the registered agent` `the certificate contains a statement that written notice of resignation was given to the corporation by mailing or delivering it at its address last known to the registered agent` `the certificate sets forth the date of the notice` `the date of the notice` `the date the certificate is filed` `the certificate includes the information last provided to the registered agent pursuant to section 132(d) for a communications contact` `the certificate is on the form prescribed by the Secretary of State` MEANS
        `the certificate is executed and acknowledged by the registered agent`
    AND `the certificate contains a statement that written notice of resignation was given to the corporation by mailing or delivering it at its address last known to the registered agent`
    AND `the certificate sets forth the date of the notice`
    AND (`the date of the notice` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 30) `before` `the date the certificate is filed`))
    AND `the certificate includes the information last provided to the registered agent pursuant to section 132(d) for a communications contact`
    AND `the certificate is on the form prescribed by the Secretary of State`

-- "Such information regarding the communications contact shall not be deemed public."
-- src:356 | Such information regarding the communications contact shall not be deemed public. A certificate filed pursuant to this section must be on the form prescribed by the Secretary of State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 136(a) (src:356)
GIVEN `the information is the information regarding the communications contact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 136(a) the information regarding the communications contact is deemed public` `the information is the information regarding the communications contact` MEANS
    FALSE

-- (b): "After receipt of the notice of the resignation of its registered agent, provided for in subsection (a) of this section, the
-- corporation for which such registered agent was acting shall obtain and designate a new registered agent to take the place of the
-- registered agent so resigning in the same manner as provided in § 133 of this title for change of registered agent."
-- src:357 | After receipt of the notice of the resignation of its registered agent, provided for in subsection (a) of this section, the corporation for which such registered agent was acting shall obtain and designate a new registered agent to take the place of the registered agent so resigning in the same manner as provided in § 133 of this title for change of registered agent. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 136(b) (src:357)
GIVEN `the corporation has received the notice of the resignation of its registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(b) the corporation must obtain and designate a new registered agent` `the corporation has received the notice of the resignation of its registered agent` MEANS
    IF   `the corporation has received the notice of the resignation of its registered agent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 136(b) Facts about the corporation` HAS
    `where the corporation is formed` IS A `Where an entity is formed`
    `the date the certificate of resignation was filed` IS A DATE
    `the date the corporation obtained and designated a new registered agent` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date as of which the question is asked` IS A DATE

-- "If such corporation, being a corporation of this State, fails to obtain and designate a new registered agent as aforesaid prior to the
-- expiration of the period of 30 days after the filing by the registered agent of the certificate of resignation, the Secretary of State
-- shall declare the charter of such corporation forfeited. If such corporation, being a foreign corporation, fails to obtain and designate
-- a new registered agent as aforesaid prior to the expiration of the period of 30 days after the filing by the registered agent of the
-- certificate of resignation, the Secretary of State shall forfeit its authority to do business in this State." A designation on the
-- thirtieth day after filing is before the expiration of the period (core Fork F3).
-- src:357 | If such corporation, being a corporation of this State, fails to obtain and designate a new registered agent as aforesaid prior to the expiration of the period of 30 days after the filing by the registered agent of the certificate of resignation, the Secretary of State shall declare the charter of such corporation forfeited. If such corporation, being a foreign corporation, fails to obtain and designate a new registered agent as aforesaid prior to the expiration of the period of 30 days after the filing by the registered agent of the certificate of resignation, the Secretary of State shall forfeit its authority to do business in this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 136(b) (src:357)
GIVEN f IS A `s 136(b) Facts about the corporation`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 136(b) the last day for the corporation to obtain and designate a new registered agent` f MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 30) `after` (f's `the date the certificate of resignation was filed`)

-- src:357 | If such corporation, being a corporation of this State, fails to obtain and designate a new registered agent as aforesaid prior to the expiration of the period of 30 days after the filing by the registered agent of the certificate of resignation, the Secretary of State shall declare the charter of such corporation forfeited. If such corporation, being a foreign corporation, fails to obtain and designate a new registered agent as aforesaid prior to the expiration of the period of 30 days after the filing by the registered agent of the certificate of resignation, the Secretary of State shall forfeit its authority to do business in this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 136(b) (src:357)
GIVEN f IS A `s 136(b) Facts about the corporation`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 132 Consequence of failing to designate a new registered agent`
`s 136(b) what follows for the corporation` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `the date the corporation obtained and designated a new registered agent`
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        IF   d AT MOST `s 136(b) the last day for the corporation to obtain and designate a new registered agent` f
        THEN JUST `the corporation is not forfeited, because it obtained and designated a new registered agent in time`
        ELSE JUST forfeiture
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF   f's `the date as of which the question is asked` AT MOST `s 136(b) the last day for the corporation to obtain and designate a new registered agent` f
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST forfeiture
    WHERE
        forfeiture MEANS
            IF   `the entity was formed under the laws of this State` (Entity WITH `kind of entity` IS `a corporation` `a stock corporation`, `where formed` IS f's `where the corporation is formed`)
            THEN `the Secretary of State declares the charter of the domestic corporation forfeited`
            ELSE `the Secretary of State forfeits the foreign corporation's qualification or authority to do business in this State`

-- (c): "After the resignation of the registered agent shall have become effective as provided in this section and if no new registered agent
-- shall have been obtained and designated in the time and manner aforesaid, service of legal process against the corporation for which the
-- resigned registered agent had been acting shall thereafter be upon the Secretary of State in accordance with § 321 of this title."
-- src:358 | (c) After the resignation of the registered agent shall have become effective as provided in this section and if no new registered agent shall have been obtained and designated in the time and manner aforesaid, service of legal process against the corporation for which the resigned registered agent had been acting shall thereafter be upon the Secretary of State in accordance with § 321 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 136(c) (src:358)
GIVEN `the resignation has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a new registered agent was obtained and designated in the time and manner required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(c) service of legal process against the corporation is upon the Secretary of State` `the resignation has become effective` `a new registered agent was obtained and designated in the time and manner required` MEANS
    IF   `the resignation has become effective` AND (NOT `a new registered agent was obtained and designated in the time and manner required`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
